# DigiStream Cline rules

Read root `AGENTS.md` first.

For every frontend/UI/UX/design-system task, read in order:

1. `docs/design/DIGISTREAM_UI_V2_COMPLETE_SPEC.md`
2. `docs/design/DIGISTREAM_UI_CONSTITUTION.md`
3. `docs/design/BEAUTIFUL_UI_ADAPTATION_STANDARD.md`
4. `docs/design/DESIGN_TOKENS.md`
5. `docs/design/DIGISTREAM_AI_IMPLEMENTATION_GUARDRAILS.md`
6. `apps/web/AGENTS.md`
7. relevant reference screens for composition/journey intent

Current visual target:

- cream dotted DigiStream canvas;
- white/warm-white operational surfaces;
- dusty-pink primary brand accent;
- restrained supporting lavender/sky/mint/amber/peach tints;
- Beautiful UI-quality compact rows/tables/search/task/loading/approval/chat/context/insight patterns;
- modern sans-serif ordinary UI;
- mono only for technical metadata/diagnostics;
- DigiStream user-visible branding.

Never restore legacy dark/emerald, blue/white, square-everything, hard-shadow-everywhere, mono-button/typewriter or giant-card rules.

Do not perform broad mechanical regex/perl/sed visual rewrites. Reconcile shared primitives, then migrate feature surfaces deliberately.

Reuse existing routes/APIs/business logic. Never fabricate product state, analytics, readiness, recordings, listener counts, permissions or success.

Do not declare UI V2 complete after foundation/token changes. Follow the completion gates in `DIGISTREAM_UI_V2_COMPLETE_SPEC.md`.
